- leaderboard/data/aes_sbox/baa9fb38c98506e2a068eb66d3d280bb807d94f9117619ff3f662f7d8c86a08f.lean
    Gate-for-gate translations (the .lean file is generated from the first .sv; the
    record's .sv and .lean are byte-identical copies of sbox_bp.sv and sbox_bp.lean; the
    _mut file, the four negatives and the attack are copies with a deliberate
    defect, each named in its header) of two AES S-box circuits published by the Circuit
    Minimization Team (Joan Boyar, René Peralta and coauthors) on
    https://www.cs.yale.edu/homes/peralta/CircuitStuff/CMT.html: the netlist files
    SLP_AES_113.txt (113 gates, depth 27; the page credits it to Cagdas Calik's
    improvement of an earlier circuit there) and AESDEPTH16SIZE125 (125 gates, depth
    16), fetched 2026-10-30. The netlist files themselves are not included
    (tests/aes_sbox/validate/validate.py fetches them and checks a pinned sha256).
    The technique: J. Boyar and R. Peralta, "A new combinational logic minimization
    technique with applications to cryptology", SEA 2010, LNCS 6049; J. Boyar,
    P. Matthews and R. Peralta, "Logic minimization techniques with applications to
    cryptology", Journal of Cryptology 26(2), 2013; J. Boyar and R. Peralta, "A small
    depth-16 circuit for the AES S-box", IFIP SEC 2012. The page states no license;
    the circuits are credited to their authors here and in each file's header.

